40.204-3 Procedures on Sudan Prohibition

L1:(a) Waivers .
L2:(1) The President may waive the certification within the provision at 52.240-90(e) on a case-by-case basis if the President determines and certifies in writing to the appropriate congressional committees that it is in the national interest to do so.
L2:(2) An agency seeking waiver of the requirement must submit the request to the Administrator of the Office of Federal Procurement Policy (OFPP), allowing sufficient time for review and approval. Upon receipt of the waiver request, OFPP must consult with the President's National Security Council and the Department of State to assess foreign policy aspects of making a national interest recommendation
L2:(3) Agencies may request a waiver on an individual or class basis; however, waivers are not indefinite and can be cancelled if warranted.
